WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.280
Hi there, welcome back.

00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:04.560
The first conversation you have with your player

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.780
can set the trajectory for the entire program.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:11.040
How do you make it count?

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.120
The goal is to establish a clear and committed partnership

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.680
from day one in what we call the commitment meeting.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.280
Now this isn't a typical check-in,

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.200
it's a dedicated session to align on expectations,

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.720
define success and agree on support.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.960
Too often, development programs fail

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.240
because of misalignment in expectations.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.340
This meeting prevents that and is the first step

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.960
in activating the manager multiplier effect.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.760
And finally, this meeting empowers you to agree on support.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.640
This is a two-way street first.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.620
Ask your player, what do you need for me

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:54.120
to be successful in this program?

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.880
A critical form of support is helping them

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:59.480
make sure they have the time to invest

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:01.200
and they make it a priority.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.600
You could offer help with protecting that space

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.840
within their work schedule.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.160
Then tell them what you need from them,

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:14.000
such as proactively sharing their insights from the course.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.240
Your play this week is simple but non-negotiable.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:20.400
Schedule and hold the commitment meeting.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:26.160
Use the agenda in your playbook to guide the conversation.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.840
During your commitment meeting,

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:31.920
your player may seem hesitant to share their goals.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:35.180
How do you apply the principles of psychological safety

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:39.360
to encourage them to open up without applying pressure?

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:42.860
Your playbook contains the first conversation guide

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.960
with key questions and prompts

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:48.140
to help you navigate this exact scenario.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.980
Review it before your meeting to ensure you're prepared

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:53.640
to build that foundation of trust.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.040
This concludes lesson one.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.240
In our next lesson, we will begin the deep work

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.140
of defining your own M.V.P. plus V blueprint.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.680
You've got this.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.560
Now, make it happen.
